    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4636" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">authepsa</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐθέψης [αὐτός ξ̓́ψω</span>, a
		self-cooker], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				utensil for cooking</i> (somewhat like our tea - urns): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in quibus (vasis) est authepsa illa, quam tanto
					pretio nuper mercatus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rosc. Am. 46, 133</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenteae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 19</span></i>
			.</div>
